    const discourse=number%2===0?
      {text:`Although the proposal addresses the immediate concern, the reviewer is not yet convinced that its benefits will last. The phrase "not yet" matters: the reviewer is asking for stronger evidence, rather than rejecting the idea. The team will record the conditions of the next trial so that the result can be compared with what happens now.`,question:choice('What does the reviewer mean by being "not yet convinced"?','The idea remains possible, but the current evidence is not sufficient.',['The idea has been rejected and a replacement has been agreed.','The evidence is accepted, but the implementation has been postponed.'],'Not yet залишає можливість змінити думку після нових доказів.')}:
      {text:`The reviewer agrees that the immediate concern needs attention. Nevertheless, agreement about the problem should not be taken as agreement about the proposed response. Two approaches may address the same issue while having different costs. The next discussion will therefore compare the recommendation with an alternative, rather than treat the first plausible idea as the final decision.`,question:choice('Why does the writer distinguish agreement about the problem from agreement about the response?','People may recognise the same problem while preferring different solutions.',['The team has changed its description of the original problem.','The reviewer accepts the response but questions whether a problem exists.'],'Розрізни визнання проблеми та підтримку конкретного рішення.')};
    if(stage>=1)reading+=`\n\nA colleague also considers another approach: ${card.contrast[2]} The discussion should make clear why the team prefers its proposed response. A useful explanation connects the choice to the situation, rather than simply saying that it is better. If the circumstances change, the team may need to review that choice.`;
